WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:06.050
Donald Trump is signing an executive order
to label Judaism a nationality. And we actually,

00:00:06.050 --> 00:00:09.540
we talked about this on yesterday's bonus
show. I wasn't planning on talking about it

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:17.410
on the broadcast show, but the amount of disinformation,
misunderstanding, and just plain old idiocy

00:00:17.410 --> 00:00:22.270
around this makes me feel like it probably
warrants a little bit more discussion today.

00:00:22.270 --> 00:00:27.880
So Trump's idea is that in order, or at least
what he's claiming is that it could be somebody

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:35.050
else's idea in order to fight antisemitism
on college campuses, you labeled Judaism and

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:41.480
nationality that will trigger a clause in
the 1964 civil rights act, which blocks federal

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:48.070
funding from any schools that allow discrimination
on the basis of nationality. That's the idea.

00:00:48.070 --> 00:00:53.399
But there are many, many issues here to talk
about. One issue of course, and it's not even

00:00:53.399 --> 00:00:57.250
the subject for today, but I find that it's
important to get on the record, some of what's

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.370
called antisemitism.

00:00:58.370 --> 00:01:05.159
On college campuses is antisemitism. Some
of it is anti Israeli organizing by people

00:01:05.159 --> 00:01:10.829
who are against Israeli foreign policy. To
be clear, there's both, and there is also

00:01:10.829 --> 00:01:15.420
stuff that's a combination of the two. That's
not the real issue for me here. The real issue

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:20.850
for me here is that Judaism simply is not
a nationality. And when you label it as such,

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:25.819
not only is it inaccurate, you're actually
perpetuating some antisemitic tropes about

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:31.929
dual loyalty that is already the source of
so much discrimination and, and attacks on

00:01:31.929 --> 00:01:37.469
Jews in the United States. So let's go through
this very carefully because it's really important

00:01:37.469 --> 00:01:44.270
that everybody understand the completely misguided
nature of this. Judaism is three things. Judaism

00:01:44.270 --> 00:01:49.999
is a religion. It's an ethnicity to the extent
that ethnicity exists, meaning I, if you go

00:01:49.999 --> 00:01:56.439
back far enough, we're all just homo sapiens.
But as ethnicity and race go, Judaism is an

00:01:56.439 --> 00:02:01.619
ethnicity and Judaism is also a cultural,
uh, group.

00:02:01.619 --> 00:02:06.170
In fact, it's more than one. You have Eastern
European jewelry, which has sort of a different

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:13.920
culture in many ways. Then Yemeni jewelry,
uh, just as as one example. So I am Jewish.

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.300
Ethnically. We actually did DNA tests on the
show. We had a DNA DNA expert come on and

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:25.450
analyze them. My results came back. I am 100%
Ashkenazi Jew. Uh, this is a sort of sub ethnic

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:31.451
group of Judaism more broadly. I can't convert
into that. I can't convert out of that. That's

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:38.989
an ethnicity. Culturally, I'm Jewish in that
I was raised in a Jewish family eating traditional

00:02:38.989 --> 00:02:44.710
Jewish foods, gathering with family around
Jewish holidays, and I am not religious. One

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:48.709
can choose to be religious or not. You can
convert into the religion of Judaism that

00:02:48.709 --> 00:02:54.739
won't make you ethnically Jewish. Of course,
now there's nothing in there about nationality.

00:02:54.739 --> 00:03:00.519
If someone discriminates against me for being
Jewish, they are maybe discriminating against

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:01.950
my ethnicity.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:06.980
They may be discriminating against my cultural
group. They might be discriminating against

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:11.700
my perceived religion, even though I'm not
religious, but there's nothing in there about

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:17.129
country of origin. In fact, I was born in
Argentina. I'm now a citizen of the United

00:03:17.129 --> 00:03:21.680
States. So when you look at my us passport,
it's an American passport. I'm an American

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.219
citizen and it says, I think, I don't remember
if it's called nationality or country of birth.

00:03:26.219 --> 00:03:31.340
It actually might be nationality on the U
S passport. Argentina. I went to Israel one

00:03:31.340 --> 00:03:38.220
time for nine days. Okay. Period. So at its
core, nothing about this is about nationality.

00:03:38.220 --> 00:03:43.689
Now there are people who are defending this
decision by Donald Trump in a mildly antisemitic

00:03:43.689 --> 00:03:52.930
way, saying Judaism is inextricably tied into
Israel because that's where the religion originates.

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:57.250
That's where Christianity also originated.
You don't see the same argument being made

00:03:57.250 --> 00:04:04.530
and as nationality is defined in the United
States, it does not fit, but it's more than

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.299
just inaccurate.

00:04:06.299 --> 00:04:11.920
When you label Judaism and nationality, it
perpetuates the antisemitic trope of dual

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:16.049
loyalty. Jews around the world and in the
United States have been dealing with this

00:04:16.049 --> 00:04:24.190
for a very long time. The idea is you're American,
but you're Jewish. So there's some hidden

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:32.430
loyalty to Israel or to Jews over country
or whatever, such that you're not really loyal

00:04:32.430 --> 00:04:37.880
to what's in the best interests of the United
States in the way that an American Christian

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:43.560
would be loyal to the United States. And this
is the source of some really, really ugly

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:50.330
stuff. So even if we take Trump, but he's
at his word, he doing this to fight antisemitism.

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:56.550
This is still a terrible idea because aside
from being factually inaccurate, it perpetuates

00:04:56.550 --> 00:05:03.020
this idea that an American born Jew who's
never been to Israel is not even religious.

00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:09.610
If discriminated against is being targeted
for their nationality. Think about how boneheaded

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:12.960
and simply incorrect that presumption would
be.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:18.699
It's wrong. It's shortsighted, it's problematic,
and hopefully Donald Trump is going to be

00:05:18.699 --> 00:05:25.000
talked out of this. Now, as with all of these
executive order things that Donald Trump does,

00:05:25.000 --> 00:05:30.470
this was unlikely to really be Trump's idea.
Uh, this is something that in all likelihood,

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:35.150
somebody came to him with and said, Hey, how
about this? What do you think about doing

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:38.030
something like this? Here's a good idea. Here's
why it would be good. This is the group that

00:05:38.030 --> 00:05:42.229
would be placated by it, or that group would
be placated by it. Let's do it. I don't even

00:05:42.229 --> 00:05:47.210
imagine for a second that Donald Trump has
any kind of deeper, serious understanding

00:05:47.210 --> 00:05:52.420
of what is implicit or, or explicit in doing
something like this. But regardless, it's

00:05:52.420 --> 00:05:56.810
a bad idea. It shouldn't be done and it doesn't
make any sense. I do want to hear from you

00:05:56.810 --> 00:06:01.639
about this. If you disagree, if you think
this is logical, let me know and try to do

00:06:01.639 --> 00:06:17.220
it without perpetuating antisemitic tropes
if possible.

00:06:17.220 --> 00:07:36.050
Right? I mean, just

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:46.379
with

00:07:46.379 --> 00:08:08.509
peace 
and love, I'm suggesting that to you.

